From 9d9b656c8100e12b56c77914bc421919b524d088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bioShaun <bioShaun@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:38:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegation): carry cumulative per-attempt usage on
 structured UPDATE

Add an optional usage snapshot { input, output, cacheRead, cacheWrite,
turns } to SubagentDelegationUpdate so a parent that cancels a child
before the terminal response can still explain cache traffic and keep
classified usage for that attempt.

- AgentProgress carries cumulative cacheRead/cacheWrite next to
  inputTokens/outputTokens/turnCount; execution updates them on every
  assistant message and after reconcileAttemptUsage.
- The progress-change gate and sameStructuredDelegationUpdateProgress
  compare all counters so a cache-only or turn-only change is not
  suppressed as a heartbeat.
- usage is projected as a fresh object only when all five counters are
  finite non-negative; missing means unavailable, not zero. tokens keeps
  its input+output meaning; the terminal response stays authoritative.
